## Arguments Reference

* `name` - (Required) Name of the user level.
* `description` - (Required) Description of the user level.
* `owner` - (Required) Identity that owns the user level. Exactly one block. Contains:
  * `id` - (Required) Owner identity ID.
  * `type` - (Optional) Owner type. Defaults to `IDENTITY`.
  * `name` - (Optional) Owner display name. When not set, the name returned by IdentityNow is used. A configured name (and type) is kept in state as long as the owner `id` does not change, so a name that differs from the display name returned by IdentityNow does not produce a diff.
* `right_sets` - (Optional) IDs of the right sets assigned to the user level, see [identitynow_authorization_right_sets](../data-sources/authorization_right_sets). When only a parent right set is listed, IdentityNow assigns all of its children as well. These children are listed in `assigned_right_sets` and do not produce a diff. A listed parent that IdentityNow only returns through its assigned children does not produce a diff either.
* `publish` - (Optional) Publish the user level after it is created or updated. Defaults to `false`, which leaves a new user level in `DRAFT` status. Setting it to `false` on a published user level has no effect.

All arguments are updated in place.

## Attributes Reference

* `id` - User level ID.
* `assigned_right_sets` - IDs of all right sets assigned to the user level, including children assigned automatically.
* `status` - Status of the user level, `DRAFT` or `ACTIVE`.
* `created` - Creation date.
* `modified` - Last modification date.

